<h1>Ransack</h1>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Ransack is fully supported but entirely optional. The engine works without any search system.</p>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Installation</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Add Ransack to your application:</p>
<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-md"><code>bundle add ransack</code></pre>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">Ransack 4+ requires you to allowlist searchable attributes on your models:</p>
<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-md"><code>class User &lt; ApplicationRecord
  def self.ransackable_attributes(_auth_object = nil)
    %w[name email created_at]
  end

  def self.ransackable_associations(_auth_object = nil)
    []
  end
end</code></pre>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Search and sort helpers</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">The engine provides helpers that wrap Ransack with styled controls. If Ransack is not installed, both helpers degrade gracefully:</p>

<ul class="l-ui-list l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
  <li>In <strong>development</strong>, a visible warning replaces the form or sort link</li>
  <li>In <strong>production</strong> and <strong>test</strong>, <code>l_ui_search_form</code> returns nothing and <code>l_ui_sort_link</code> renders a plain-text header cell; both log a warning</li>
</ul>

<div class="l-ui-container--table l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
  <table class="l-ui-table">
    <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Available helpers</caption>
    <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Helper</th>
        <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l_ui_search_form</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Styled search form wrapping Ransack's <code>search_form_for</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th class="l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><code>l_ui_sort_link</code></th>
        <td class="l-ui-table__cell">Styled sort link wrapping Ransack's <code>sort_link</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Search example</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Search users by name or email:</p>

<%= l_ui_search_form(@q, url: ransack_path, fields: [:name, :email], clear: true) %>

<% if params[:q].present? && @users.present? %>
  <div class="l-ui-container--table l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
    <table class="l-ui-table">
      <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Search results</caption>
      <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
        <tr>
          <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Name</th>
          <th class="l-ui-table__header-cell" scope="col">Email</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
        <% @users.each do |user| %>
          <tr>
            <th class="l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><%= user.name %></th>
            <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><%= user.email %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% elsif params[:q].present? %>
  <p class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">No users found matching your search.</p>
<% end %>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Sorting example</h2>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-md">Click column headers to sort. The helper wraps Ransack's <code>sort_link</code> and applies the <code>l-ui-table__sort-link</code> class automatically.</p>

<div class="l-ui-container--table l-ui-utility--mt-lg">
  <table class="l-ui-table">
    <caption class="l-ui-sr-only">Sortable users</caption>
    <thead class="l-ui-table__header">
      <tr>
        <%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :name) %>
        <%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :email) %>
        <%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :created_at, "Joined", default_order: :desc) %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="l-ui-table__body">
      <% @users.each do |user| %>
        <tr>
          <th class="l-ui-table__cell--primary" scope="row"><%= user.name %></th>
          <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><%= user.email %></td>
          <td class="l-ui-table__cell"><%= time_ago_in_words(user.created_at) %> ago</td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="l-ui-utility--mt-2xl">Sort link usage</h2>

<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-md"><code>&lt;!-- Basic sort link --&gt;
&lt;%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :name) %&gt;

&lt;!-- Custom label --&gt;
&lt;%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :created_at, "Joined") %&gt;

&lt;!-- Default descending order --&gt;
&lt;%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :created_at, "Joined", default_order: :desc) %&gt;

&lt;!-- With HTML options --&gt;
&lt;%= l_ui_sort_link(@q, :name, html: { data: { turbo_action: "replace" } }) %&gt;</code></pre>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">In your controller, let Ransack handle ordering:</p>

<pre class="l-ui-surface l-ui-utility--mt-md"><code>def index
  @q = User.ransack(params[:q])
  @users = @q.result(distinct: true)
  @users = @users.order(:name) if @q.sorts.empty?
end</code></pre>

<p class="l-ui-utility--mt-lg">See the <%= link_to "search page", search_path %> for the full search helper API, options, and partials reference.</p>
